From 5507a2e9f24827ff5cc58890140780633df9fbd6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 18:06:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 16/32] generate: an overlapped read never pads a group up over
 a parked conversation; a read's CUDA fault releases the spin waits

Two review findings on STRATA_PIPE_OVERLAP=1 (env off: unchanged).

- A group started during an overlapped read whose own layout was missing ran padded up to the full width; the pad
  rows in [S0, GS) wrote slots the run without the overlap never touches, so a conversation parked there (a request
  that ended, BDONE, or a BYIELD's partial read) lost its slot cache and its next turn read its prompt again. ov_layout
  now takes the group's own width, else the narrowest wider layout every stage holds whose extra rows park no
  conversation (cached or partial; the slot being read into is overwritten anyway), else the group waits for the read's
  end. overlap_prepare also captures, for each active group, every width it may shrink to during the read (1 .. its
  own width; Verifier::ensure_batch_layouts takes them as `narrow`, held ones marked as used for an LRU limit), so
  pad-ups and waits become rare: batch_overlap_test went from 123 pad-ups per run to 0.
- A CUDA fault the read's threads saw left read_overlapped without releasing the stages' GPU waits, while a window
  the last pump started on stage 0 could still spin on its PLE flag at #224's _Exit (#267). The fault branch now
  aborts through the guard (release_gpu_waits on every stage, with its watchdog allowance) first and logs it.
- STRATA_PIPE_OVERLAP_TEST_FAULT=cuda: the read reports a CUDA fault after its read (fault path d, on a sound context).
- tools/batch_overlap_test.py: G ends while H is read and G's next turn (G2) must continue from G's slot (its RESUME);
  --compare checks every request's RESUME too.

Checked (T16-mmqtab.json, split 12,24,36, STRATA_MMQ_DIRECT=1, --pcie-frac 0 --adapt-every 1000000
--no-prefill-borrow, STRATA_IQ_MT_MIN=1): the new case fails on the previous engine with FORCE_PADUP=1 (G2 RESUME 0);
batch_overlap_test passes with the env on, off, FORCE_PADUP=1 and FORCE_WAIT=2, token- and RESUME-identical across
them and to the reference engine's tokens; the cuda fault arm passes (one ERR, rc 1, no watchdog); batch_test16 env
off and on: 16/16 identical to solo, env off identical to the reference engine's dump.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
